"""
Connector-template catalog: seeded into, and read back from, PostgreSQL.

On startup we (1) ensure the dc_connector_templates table exists and (2)
seed it from TEMPLATE_SEED if empty. PostgreSQL is the only copy of this
data — app/services/catalog_service.py reads it directly on every request,
there is no in-memory cache to warm.

If the database is unreachable, this retries for a while (Postgres in a
freshly-started stack can take a few seconds to accept connections) and
raises if it never comes up — app/startup.py treats a failed seed/template
check as fatal before the API ever starts, so the service fails readiness
rather than serving with no template catalog at all.
"""

import asyncio

import structlog
from sqlalchemy import func, select

